# 4. The column names are changed to meaningful names such as buying, maint, doors, persons, lug_boot, safety and class.
# 5. Label Encoding converts categorical values into numerical values so the Random Forest model can process them.
# 6. The dataset is split into training data to build the model and testing data to evaluate its predictions.
# 7. Random Forest combines predictions from multiple decision trees to classify cars into unacc, acc, good or vgood categories.
